 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Musa, Isa and Maryam: no motif at all. The crucifixion is never drawn. 157:10-16 says only what both tafsirs say: they did not kill or crucify him; another man was made to resemble him and was crucified (As-Sa'di: «بل شبه لهم غيره، فقتلوا غيره وصلبوه»). Their claim in 157:1-9 is glossed as mockery, never as a statement. 156 states Maryam's innocence. A door for «الباب», a seal for «ميثاقا»; no mountain over them, no calf. Al-Muyassar's first-person «فلعناهم» not used."
